sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as MCP Client<br/>(Claude, Cursor, etc.)
    participant ClientHost as Client Metadata Host<br/>(https://client.example/.well-known/oauth-client)
    participant Proxy as MCP Auth Adapter
    participant SSO as Upstream IdP
    participant MCPServer as MCP Server

    Note over Client, MCPServer: 1. Discovery
    Client->>MCPServer: Connects to server
    MCPServer-->>Client: Announces MCP Auth Adapter as Authorization Server
    Client->>Proxy: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    Proxy->>SSO: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    SSO-->>Proxy: Returns descriptor
    Proxy-->>Client: Returns filtered descriptor (issuer=adapter, iss_supported=true,<br/>authorization/token endpoints=adapter, CIMD supported)

    Note over Client, SSO: 2. Authorization with CIMD client_id and RFC 9207 iss verification
    Client->>Proxy: GET /authorize (client_id=https://client.example/..., scopes, redirect_uri)
    Proxy->>ClientHost: GET https://client.example/.well-known/oauth-client (fetch CIMD metadata)
    ClientHost-->>Proxy: Returns CIMD JSON (client_id, redirect_uris, client_name, ...)
    Note over Proxy: Validates CIMD document (client_id match, redirect_uri match)<br/>Resolves CIMD URL → upstream client_id via configured map<br/>Filters scopes, signs state blob
    Proxy-->>Client: 302 → Upstream IdP /authorize<br/>(substituted client_id, redirect_uri=adapter/callback, state=signed_blob)
    Client->>SSO:  GET /authorize (substituted client_id, redirect_uri=adapter/callback, state=signed_blob)
    Note over SSO: Authenticates user, consent screen shown
    SSO-->>Client: 302 → adapter/authorize/callback?code=X&state=signed_blob&iss=upstream_issuer

    Client->>Proxy: GET /authorize/callback?code=X&state=signed_blob&iss=upstream_issuer
    Note over Proxy: Verifies HMAC signature & expiration<br/>Validates upstream iss parameter<br/>Extracts original redirect_uri and state
    Proxy-->>Client: 302 → client_callback?code=X&state=client_state&iss=adapter_issuer
    Note over Client: Validates iss to be adapter_issuer<br/>from the discovered descriptor

    Note over Client, SSO: 3. Token Exchange with CIMD client_id
    Client->>Proxy: POST /token (client_id=https://client.example/..., code, redirect_uri)
    Note over Proxy: Validates CIMD URL, resolves to upstream client_id<br/>Rewrites redirect_uri to adapter/callback
    Proxy->>SSO: POST /token (substituted upstream client_id, redirect_uri=adapter/callback)
    Note over SSO: Validates redirect_uri to be the same as during Authorization
    SSO-->>Proxy: Returns Access Token (+ Refresh Token)
    Proxy-->>Client: Relays token response

    Note over Client, MCPServer: 4. Secure Resource Access & Access Token Validation
    Client->>MCPServer: Sends MCP request (e.g. tool call) with Access Token
    MCPServer->>Proxy: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    Proxy-->>MCPServer: Returns descriptor containing JWKS (Certificate) URI from Upstream IdP
    MCPServer-->>SSO: Fetches Certificate used to sign Access Token
    MCPServer->>MCPServer: Validates the Access Token signature & claims<br/>Authenticates and authorizes request
